The SMF shall proceed with the UUAA-SM procedure and refrain from accepting or rejecting the request until service-level authentication and authorization completes when all of the following apply:

- the PDU session is **non-emergency**;
- the request type is **not** “existing PDU session”;
- the **Service-level-AA container IE** is included in the **PDU SESSION ESTABLISHMENT REQUEST**;
- service-level authentication and authorization by the external DN is required by local policy;
- valid subscription information exists for the requested DNN, or requested DNN and S-NSSAI; and
- the Service-level-AA container includes the **CAA-level UAV ID**.

“The UE can request the use of both MICO mode with active time and eDRX during a registration procedure but it is up to the network to decide to enable none, one of them or both.”

Thus, the network may enable:

- neither MICO mode with active time nor eDRX;
- MICO mode with active time only;
- eDRX only; or
- both MICO mode with active time and eDRX.

For 5GMM cause **#3 “Illegal UE”**, the UE shall:

- set 5GS update status to **5U3 ROAMING NOT ALLOWED**;
- delete any **5G-GUTI, last visited registered TAI, TAI list, and ngKSI**;
- in a PLMN, consider the **USIM invalid for 5GS services** until switch-off, UICC removal, or expiry of T3245; and
- if not registered for SNPN onboarding services, delete the equivalent-PLMN list and enter **5GMM-DEREGISTERED.NO-SUPI**.

Because the SERVICE REJECT is **not integrity protected**, the UE does **not** perform the actions explicitly conditional on successful NAS integrity checking, e.g. setting the relevant invalid-credential/attempt counters to their maximum or deleting the stored 5GMM parameters in non-volatile memory.
